{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791044349,"nonce":"x97dvmRRs477xSLnTHkhwXAovXA=","title":"AOT stores hl.Bytes in a Dynamic slot unboxed","message":"Reported by the ChimpMonk session against v0.1.2 (9a07b98) and 643fc3c: iterating an Array\u003chl.Bytes\u003e under `ash --build` reads each element as null (zeroed buffers) or garbage (real data; their case segfaulted in hlp_dyn_castp at 0xffffffff). interp, jit and hybrid are correct.\n\nCause: the LLVM lowering's ToDyn copied every pointer into the Dynamic unboxed except HABSTRACT, and the virtual-call argument boxing in calls.rs did the same. hl.Bytes has no hl_type header, so the SafeCast back out read the buffer's first word as a type. Cranelift boxes everything outside the runtime's hl_is_dynamic set (HDYN, HFUN, HOBJ, HARRAY, HVIRTUAL, HDYNOBJ, HENUM, HNULL), which is why jit was right; the LLVM tier inside jit had the same bug but this program never got hot enough to reach it.\n\nFix: one shared predicate, `types::kind_is_dynamic`, used by Cranelift and both LLVM sites. Repro (theirs): /tmp/ash-aot-bytes-array-repro.hx; regression: crates/ash/test/tests/TestDynBytes.hx in the aot_smoke corpus.","files":null}]}